sourceText:
Mira Okafor @mira_builds
We're paying 5 devs to make a YouTube tutorial with Lattice (our open-source vector search for edge functions). Here's the deal 🧵

1/ Build something real with lattice-sdk v0.9 or newer. RAG over your own docs, semantic search for a blog, a recipe finder, whatever you like. It must actually run on Cloudflare Workers or Vercel Edge.

2/ Record a tutorial: at least 8 minutes, landscape, screen + your own voice, you writing the code (not just scrolling through a finished repo). Face cam optional.

3/ Publish it publicly on your own YouTube channel. The title has to include the word Lattice. Put the public GitHub repo and the deployed URL in the description.

4/ Upload between June 3 and June 28. Anything published before June 3 doesn't count, sorry.

5/ Five slots. The first five videos that meet the bar get paid, in USDC. We don't care about subscriber count, a 0-sub channel is fine if the video is good.

6/ Disqualified: AI voiceover, lattice-sdk below 0.9 (the old createIndex API), a repo that doesn't build, unlisted or private videos, Shorts.

7/ Reply with in and I'll add you to the list. Questions in the replies or docs.lattice.dev/discord

Replies
@devjunaid: in. can I use bun on workers?
@mira_builds: @devjunaid yes, as long as it deploys to Workers
@k8sKat: does a short count?
@mira_builds: @k8sKat no, 8 min minimum, landscape
@ana_codes: in! can it be in Spanish?
@mira_builds: @ana_codes yes, any language is fine, the code just has to be real
